        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "ci: clear agent lint and browser dead export",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMain CI exposed two unrelated regressions while landing the transient cleanup fix:\n\n- `src/agents/model-fallback.test.ts` violated `preserve-caught-error` by replacing a caught non-Error rejection without retaining it.\n- `BrowserRouteHandler` remained exported after production dead-export baselines were tightened.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe abortable test helper now attaches the original rejection as the replacement Error's `cause`. The browser route handler alias is module-private, while the test helper derives the equivalent handler type from `BrowserRouteRegistrar`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNone. CI and internal type-surface cleanup only.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Main lint failure: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29298071103/job/86976084021\n- Exact-head dependency failure: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29298553806/job/86977331802\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxf3dnge45p65hkdp89gjr57`, Actions `29298341138`: initial changed gate passed; lint zero warnings/errors.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxf3y6mzab13jah7yb6sgksp`, Actions `29298711603`: dead exports matched the 1,167-entry baseline; full changed gate passed, including formatting, types, core/extensions lint, plugin SDK baseline, and import-cycle checks.\n- Fresh autoreview clean at 0.98 confidence after the final formatting change.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n",
